I am the core maintainer of Ai-assitance-stock-learning, an open-source public repository focused on leveraging artificial intelligence for stock market analysis and machine learning models. As the project expands, managing algorithmic code validation, triaging community bugs, and checking data pipeline security has become a bottleneck. Free Codex access will allow me to automate code reviews, write test suites, and accelerate the development of our stock forecasting features.

# Ai-assitance-stock-learning

An open-source Python repository designed to leverage artificial intelligence and machine learning models for stock market analysis, predictive modeling, and financial data exploration.

## 🚀 Key Features
* **AI Predictive Modeling**: Machine learning algorithms applied to historical stock trends.
* **Data Pipelines**: Automated fetching and cleaning of financial market data.
* **Technical Indicators**: Integration of core financial metrics for model training.

## 🛠️ Built With
* [Python](https://python.org) - Core programming language
* Data libraries (Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-Learn)

## 💻 Installation & Setup

Clone the repository to your local machine:
```bash
git clone https://github.com
cd Ai-assitance-stock-learning
```

